# Getting Started

This guide will help you set up and start using the {{ project_slug }} ML template.

## Prerequisites

- Python 3.12+
- Git
- (Optional) CUDA-compatible GPU for accelerated training

## Installation

### 1. Install uv

First, install uv if you haven't already:

```bash
# On macOS and Linux
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh

# On Windows
powershell -c "irm https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1 | iex"
```

### 2. Clone and Setup Project

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone {{ repo_url }}
cd {{ project_slug }}

# Install Python 3.14
uv python install 3.14
uv python pin 3.14

{%- if use_torch %}

# Install dependencies with CUDA support (Ubuntu/Linux)
uv sync --group dev --group docs --extra cu126

# For CPU-only installation
uv sync --group dev --group docs --extra cpu
{%- else %}

# Install dependencies
uv sync --group dev --group docs
{%- endif %}
```

### 3. Verify Installation

Test the installation by running:

```bash
# Test CLI
uv run {{ project_slug }}-cli hello

# Run tests
uv run pytest
```

